ucation. Also C's communication difficulty could be serious.\n\nWe need to weigh which is more critical. Communication is crucial. Egocentric may affect crew cooperation. But D's moody/loner could also affect. However we have no evidence of D's behavior affecting crew. C's communication difficulty is documented. So perhaps D is safer.\n\nWe also have not discussed Candidate A at all. Could bring A as a point, but we need to keep discussion systematic. Perhaps we can say we still have concerns about D's moody/loner traits and lack of evidence doesn't guarantee safety, but we need more info. However we might still keep C.\n\nGiven we need to move toward convergence, we could propose a compromise: maybe we need to weigh which risk is higher. We could ask for more evidence about D's teamwork. But we have already asked and got no evidence. So we could argue that D's interpersonal concerns are less concrete than C's communication difficulty, thus D is preferable.\n\nThus we could shift our vote to D, aligning with Agent 1, and provide reasoning.\n\nWe must reference prior discussion: Agent 2's point about C's strengths, Agent 1's point about D's strengths and lack of hot temper evidence, and Sofia's own earlier note about B's numeric weakness. Also we can mention that we still have no evidence of D's hot temper, and his responsibility and concentration are critical.\n\nThus we will change vote to Candidate D.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with Anna that D's strengths outweigh C's communication issues, and I shift my vote to D.\" Provide evidence: D's concentration, problem solving, responsibility, no hot temper evidence; C's difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric attitude.\n\nNow METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate D.\n\nProceed."}
