haps, and see if A could be a better fit. That would be a new point but still connected: we can say \"While I support D, we still haven't examined Candidate A, whose leadership and anticipation of dangerous situations could be valuable, but his unorganized nature and poor response to criticism raise reliability concerns.\" Then we can state whether that changes our recommendation. Likely we still recommend D, but we note A is not as strong. So we keep vote D.\n\nThus we need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: agree with D, note A still under-discussed, but A's issues (unorganized, poor criticism) make him less suitable than D. So we keep D.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote D.\n\nProceed."}
